cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OmniOmics: an integrated desktop environment for reproducible multi-omics analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Angelo Felipe"
    family-names: "Barbosa de Oliveira"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0831-447X"
    affiliation: "Programa de Pós-Graduação em Genética e Biologia Molecular, Universidade Federal do Pará (UFPA), Belém, PA, Brazil"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliv-angelus/OmniOmics"
abstract: >-
  OmniOmics is a desktop application that packages five Snakemake workflows for
  metagenomics (MAGMA), isolate genomics (SIGMA), metatranscriptomics (DOGMA),
  differential expression (DEFINE) and amplicon metabarcoding (PRISM) behind a
  graphical interface, together with an integrated plotting environment that
  turns each workflow's output into publication-ready figures. It is aimed at
  researchers who need reproducible multi-omics analysis without assembling and
  maintaining the toolchain by hand. All five pipelines were validated end to
  end on real, non-simulated public datasets against independent, external
  ground truth (certified mock-community compositions, reference genomes,
  published papers' own reported results, and a sequencing vendor's own
  classification of the same read file); the exact configuration, ground
  truth, and results are published at github.com/oliv-angelus/
  OmniOmics-validation and reported in the accompanying manuscript.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - metagenomics
  - metatranscriptomics
  - amplicon sequencing
  - Snakemake
  - reproducibility
